  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The acidic character of hypohalous acid depends on the electronegativity of halogen. As the electronegativity value of halogen increases the acidic strength of hypohalous acid increases.<br /><br />Here, Electronegativity of atom <math> <mtext>X</mtext></math> (<math> <mrow>  <mtext>Cl,</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>Br</mtext></mrow></math> or <math> <mtext>I</mtext></math>) attached to <math> <mtext>O</mtext></math> decreases down the group, polarity of OH bond decreases, acid strength decreases. It means more the electronegativity of the halogen atom, more the tendency to pull electron and weaker the <math> <mrow>  <mtext>O</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo><mtext>H</mtext></mrow></math> bond and hence proton <math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mtext>(H</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>+</mtext>  </msup>  <mtext>)</mtext></mrow></math> can easily be removed.",
    "image": null
  },
